('EM-TKT-INS-1011-20260911-6-1', 'TKT-INS-1011-20260911-6', 'INS-1011', 'arun.mehta@hdfc.com', 'INBOUND', 'arun.mehta@hdfc.com', 'support@bharatsuraksha.co.in', 'Cashless pre-authorisation delay', 'Dear Sir/Madam,

I am writing with reference to policy POL-5015. My cashless pre-authorisation request for claim CLM-3009 is still showing as "under review" on your portal.

The hospital has told me they cannot proceed on cashless basis without the approval letter. The estimated amount is INR 210,000. I have already submitted the discharge summary, the treating doctor''s note and the pre-auth form through your TPA portal.

Please confirm when the approval will be issued.

Regards,
Arun Mehta
Policy POL-5015', 1, '2026-09-11 16:00:00'),
('EM-TKT-INS-1011-20260911-6-2', 'TKT-INS-1011-20260911-6', 'INS-1011', 'arun.mehta@hdfc.com', 'OUTBOUND', 'support@bharatsuraksha.co.in', 'arun.mehta@hdfc.com', 'Cashless pre-authorisation delay', 'Dear Arun,

Thank you for writing in. Your request has been registered under ticket TKT-INS-1011-20260911-6.

We have escalated the pre-authorisation to our TPA for review. The standard turnaround is 48 working hours from receipt of complete documentation.

Regards,
Customer Service
Bharat Suraksha Health Insurance', 2, '2026-09-12 12:00:00'),
('EM-TKT-INS-1011-20260911-6-3', 'TKT-INS-1011-20260911-6', 'INS-1011', 'arun.mehta@hdfc.com', 'INBOUND', 'arun.mehta@hdfc.com', 'support@bharatsuraksha.co.in', 'Cashless pre-authorisation delay', 'This is the third time I am writing.

It has now been well past the 48 hours you quoted. The hospital is asking me to settle in cash and claim reimbursement later, which defeats the entire purpose of a cashless policy that I have paid INR 65,000 a year for.

I want a written explanation of the delay and the name of the officer handling this. If I do not receive the approval today I will be raising this with the IRDAI grievance cell.

Arun Mehta', 3, '2026-09-14 20:00:00'),
('EM-TKT-INS-1011-20260911-6-4', 'TKT-INS-1011-20260911-6', 'INS-1011', 'arun.mehta@hdfc.com', 'OUTBOUND', 'support@bharatsuraksha.co.in', 'arun.mehta@hdfc.com', 'Cashless pre-authorisation delay', 'Dear Arun,

We acknowledge the delay and sincerely regret the inconvenience. Ticket TKT-INS-1011-20260911-6 has been marked urgent and assigned to a senior claims officer.

We will revert within 24 hours.

Regards,
Customer Service', 4, '2026-09-15 00:00:00'),
('EM-TKT-INS-1011-20260920-7-1', 'TKT-INS-1011-20260920-7', 'INS-1011', 'arun.mehta@hdfc.com', 'INBOUND', 'arun.mehta@hdfc.com', 'support@bharatsuraksha.co.in', 'Deficiency letter — documents already submitted', 'Dear Sir/Madam,

I have received a deficiency letter on claim CLM-3009 asking for the same documents I have already uploaded twice — the discharge summary and the final bill.

This is the second deficiency letter on the same claim. Each time the clock appears to restart. Please confirm what is genuinely outstanding so I can close this once.

Regards,
Arun Mehta', 1, '2026-09-20 17:00:00'),
('EM-TKT-INS-1011-20260920-7-2', 'TKT-INS-1011-20260920-7', 'INS-1011', 'arun.mehta@hdfc.com', 'OUTBOUND', 'support@bharatsuraksha.co.in', 'arun.mehta@hdfc.com', 'Deficiency letter — documents already submitted', 'Dear Arun,

Ticket TKT-INS-1011-20260920-7 refers. We have asked the TPA to reconcile the documents received against the deficiency raised and revert.

Regards,
Claims Support', 2, '2026-09-21 23:00:00'),
